 Member 2 (Geneticist): Assesses any potential genetic factors contributing to congenital heart diseases, offering insights into the etiology of the newborn’s condition and counseling for any family history of congenital anomalies that may relate to the diagnosis.
 Member 3 (Pediatric Critical Care Specialist): Oversees the sophisticated management of a critically ill newborn, advising on ventilation strategies and other intensive care measures related to the evolving respiratory failure, particularly in the context of reducing pulmonary vascular resistance and optimizing hemodynamics.

Group 3 -  Final Review and Decision Team (FRDT)
 Member 1 (Senior Pediatric Cardiologist (Lead)): Provides an overarching perspective on the case, coordinating the synthesis of all data gathered from the IAT and DET to confirm the differential diagnosis and management plan.
 Member 2 (Pediatric Surgeon): Works in conjunction with the cardiologist to finalize surgical options, timings, and preparations necessary for a definitive corrective procedure following the atrial septostomy.
 Member 3 (Clinical Pathologist): Reviews and integrates laboratory results that may influence surgical decisions and postoperative management, ensuring that all biological and diagnostic data are adequately represented in the final planning.


